# Decimal subtraction preserves operand scale

Subtracts 1.20 from 2.30 to verify the difference keeps the two-digit
fractional scale shared by its operands, producing 1.10.

>>> source
decimal_left: decimal = 2.30
decimal_right: decimal = 1.20

decimal_diff: decimal = decimal_left - decimal_right
print(decimal_diff)

<<< stdout
1.10

<<< stderr
